  "body": "See https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5574#issuecomment-639385987\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#current-pixel-density is a property of image request, not `img`.\r\n\r\nEditorial spec bugs that make this unclear:\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#image-request\r\n\r\n> An image request has a state, current URL, and image data.\r\n\r\nThis should mention \"current pixel density\".\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#images-processing-model:current-pixel-density\r\n\r\n> When an img element has a current pixel density that is not 1.0\r\n\r\nThis should say \"When an img element's current request has a current pixel density that is not 1.0\"\r\n\r\nThere might be further cases like this, I haven't stepped through all instances of \"current pixel density\".",
